# Security Rules

## Mandatory

- Server-side Zod validation on all inputs
- Server-side price calculation — never trust client prices
- `clientQuotedTotalMinor` is informational only
- Verify entity IDs exist and are active before use
- `assertExtraCustomerSelectable` for customer-requested extras
- Use `serverEnv` / `clientEnv` — never bare `process.env`
- `toPublicError()` before sending errors to client
- `import "server-only"` on server modules
- `Idempotency-Key` header required for reservation creation

## Forbidden

- Exposing secrets in client bundles
- Leaking stack traces, SQL errors, or internal paths
- Trusting client-supplied entity relationships
- Skipping validation because "the client already validated"
- Business logic in Route Handlers
- Notification calls inside DB transactions
- Returning customer PII in public reservation responses

## Rate limiting

- Postgres-backed via `rate_limit_buckets`
- Applied in Route Handlers only
- Quote: 30/min/IP; Reservation: 10/hr/IP + 5/hr/email

## Anti-spam

- Honeypot field (`website` must be empty)
- Minimum form fill time (3 seconds)
- Turnstile extension point (not mandatory in Phase 3)

## Before modifying security-sensitive code

Read `/docs/SECURITY.md`.
